From b20fc6a48590b202dce9a0f90b9a0eab5f7ab275 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:25:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make silk.compress.deflate write zlib's bytes and inflate
 report zlib's causes

deflate: steps follow zlib 1.3.1's deflate() call for call, level 0 is zlib's
deflate_stored, and dictionaries, parameter changes, the window slide and the
match search keep the state zlib keeps, so the compressed bytes and the input
and output of each step are zlib's. Encoder.setGzipSystem sets the gzip
operating system byte. The match search reads through pointers and compares
eight bytes at a time; the hash insert is inlined.

inflate: Decoder.failureDetail gives zlib's cause of a failure; headers are
checked in zlib's units; Decoder.setWindowBits, setMemberStop and setBlockStop
give what inflateInit2, a single gzip member and Z_BLOCK give; a full output
leaves the input zlib leaves.

corpus/native/deflate-zlib-bytes checks bytes that zlib 1.3.1 wrote, through
16 ways to cut the steps, and the new decoder options.
